              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Andrew Fender"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This turned out well enough, though not without some issues. One hour was hardly enough to firm up the meatballs. Two hours seemed to work fine, though. I would also have liked it better if the sauce had reduced at all, or if it tasted good enough to make the whole thing function like a soup. As it is though, it's good, but could be better.",
            "datePublished": "2021-11-26T03:56:09.547Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "1"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AutismMom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Not good. Instead of using the jar of salsa, substitute it for bottle of Hunt's chili sauce, and mix with the grape jelly (don't use jam!). I make my meatballs differently, breadcrumbs, parmesan, parsley, and a splash of Worcestershire sauce and milk.",
